course: dictionary
lesson: 7471
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The everyday meaning of porridge is a warm, soft food made by cooking oats in milk or water until thick. «Porridge, toast, cereal and fruit give steady energy before sport.» The sentence is about breakfast and energy, so porridge is food.
explain: The second meaning is old British slang: «doing porridge» means being in prison. In the sentence «By 1908 most prisoners were held in purpose-built prisons... prison food was plain, like bread, porridge and potatoes», porridge is the food served to prisoners. To check, put your meaning into the sentence. Does «prison food was plain, like food made from oats» make sense? Yes, so the food meaning fits.
explain: Clues like hungry and after their porridge show the meaning. «At lunch-time the two hedgehogs, hungry again after their porridge, looked up at the Badger without speaking.» You do not need the slang meaning here, because the hedgehogs are simply hungry and have eaten porridge.
fact: Porridge is a warm, soft food made by cooking oats in milk or water until it is thick.
fact: In the USA, porridge is usually called «oatmeal».
fact: In British slang, «doing porridge» means being in prison. It is an old joke, not used at school.
fact: In «Goldilocks and the Three Bears», one bowl of porridge is too hot, one is too cold and one is just right.
fact: Porridge is uncountable, so you say «some porridge», not «three porridges».
exercise: «Porridge, toast, cereal and fruit give steady energy before sport.» What is porridge in this sentence? | * A warm food made from oats | A type of fruit | A kind of sport | A prison cell
exercise: What does «doing porridge» mean in British slang? | Playing a game outside | * Being in prison | Cooking in a hot pan | Eating a big breakfast
exercise: What is porridge made by cooking? | Olives | Fish sauce | Dormice | * Oats in milk or water
test: In the USA, what is porridge usually called? | Dumplings | Cereal | Toast | * Oatmeal
test: Which phrase uses porridge as slang for prison? | porridge with honey | * doing porridge | a bowl of porridge | porridge oats
exam: «Ordinary Romans ate bread, porridge, olives, cheese and vegetables.» What is porridge in this sentence? | * A warm food made from cooked grain | A kind of dormouse | A rich feast lying on couches | A type of prison
